INT. ROOFTOP HELIPAD, UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL - DAWN

Wind whips the windsock. The city below is a quilt of pink and gray. A helicopter idles on the pad, rotors turning slow.

Three staff stand by a wheeled cooler: DR. IMANI OKAFOR-REYES (40s, flight suit), NURSE ALARIC BRIGHTWATER-LUU (30s, backpack), and TRANSPLANT COORDINATOR SERAPHINA KOWALSKI-ASANTE (50s, headset). The cooler contains a donor heart.

IMANI
(to everyone)
Okay. Last check. Cooler sealed? Ice good? Paperwork in?

ALARIC
Sealed. Ice good. Paperwork in.

SERAPHINA
(into headset)
Control, we are loaded. Requesting clearance.

SERAPHINA (CONT'D)
(to the others)
Four minutes.

IMANI
(to herself)
Four minutes. I can do four minutes.

The rotors whine. Alaric lifts the cooler's handle, lowers it, lifts it again.

ALARIC
Doctor, can I ask something?

IMANI
Go.

ALARIC
Is it supposed to feel this heavy?

IMANI
Yes.

ALARIC
Is it supposed to feel this light?

IMANI
Also yes.

SERAPHINA
Clearance in thirty.

IMANI
Then let's go.

She steps toward the helicopter. Alaric steps after her. Seraphina pulls off her headset, takes a breath, and walks to the pad's edge. She looks down at the waking city. Then, quietly, to the empty air:

SERAPHINA (CONT'D)
(to the donor)
Thank you.

The rotors speed up. The sun clears the buildings. And somewhere in the cooler, nothing moves at all.
